From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lars Trieloff <lars@trieloff.net>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:34:18 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 02/13] providers: build only age and plain for WASI

The provider generator takes an allowlist on WASI targets. Disabled
providers keep their configuration variants, so every fnox.toml still
parses, and fail at instantiation with "provider type '<type>' is not
available in the WASI build of fnox". Their modules, the hardware-key
setup paths and age plugin support are compiled out on WASI, and
BitwardenBackend is kept as a plain enum for the configuration types.

Disabled providers also keep their env_dependencies(), read at build
time from the compiled-out module's source (the build fails if that is
not a literal list), so `proxy run` still removes a configured
provider's credentials (FNOX_OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN, FNOX_BW_SESSION,
VAULT_NAMESPACE, ...) from the child, and the resolver orders by them,
as upstream does (homescoop#401). A provider module may be a directory
(lua/mod.rs), and a list may be a named constant from a provider
module (the Azure providers' SERVICE_PRINCIPAL_ENV_VARS, from
azure_shared): the build reads that constant's literal list.

1.40.0 adds the kubernetes and lua providers, both compiled out on
WASI like the other remote ones; the lua provider's plugin lookup is
skipped there, so a lua provider fails like any disabled one.
azure_shared, which the Azure providers and the azure-token lease
backend share since 1.40.0, stays built for its environment variable
list and service_principal_env(); its Azure SDK credential code is
compiled out.

